      "message": "Let something ask whether the forge is up, and say so when the answer changes\n\nA forge cannot report its own absence. `cairn admin watch` is the thing\nthat asks: one look per invocation, the answer remembered in a state\nfile, mail only when the answer changes and once a day while it stays\ndown, a non-zero exit while down so the timer that runs it shows the same.\nIt uses the mail the forge already has, so a watcher on any machine with\nthe binary and the relay settings is enough; it depends on nothing but\nthe forge it watches.\n\nThe operating guide gains the section, and the first-run walk ends by\nwatching the forge it used: up while serving, down once stopped, the\noutage remembered as news. Beside it, scripts/upload-s3.py puts a backup\nbundle into any S3-compatible bucket with python and curl alone, so the\ncopy off the machine needs no client installed.\n\nChange-Id: Iwatch0088liveness\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
